{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4H5DJVvp6T8p9KXimG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the one real stub and checked the mouse controls. The rest of the stop hook's list is a mismatch with TASK.md, as follows.\n\n**Changes just made**\n- **Boot steps:** they were empty functions. They now do real work: building the commentator portraits, loading the records and cup save, and applying the balance sliders.\n- **Mouse controls:** these were only partly tested before. A new browser test (`test/mouse.mjs`) now checks that hovering finds a teammate, a left click passes to them, and holding then releasing the right button kicks. All three pass.\n- **Suite:** `node test/all.mjs` now runs five suites and 126 checks, all passing. The single `.html` is rebuilt in the root.\n\n**Points I'm not changing**\n- **Behind-the-kicker camera:** this is PLAN.md's idea, and PLAN.md's own fallback is an aim gauge on the broadcast view, which is what ships. TASK.md says it wins where they disagree and doesn't require that camera. Scrums, lineouts, penalties and goal kicks all work as playable systems.\n- **Xbox glyphs:** I screenshotted them and they render, but I haven't tried them on real hardware, and I'm leaving that line as it stood. There is no stub behind it.\n- **Feedback text:** I wrote those answers from this session, and the generator script only keeps `exit-interview.json` and the in-game About screen in sync. The `usage` field is \"unknown\" because no token or cost estimate is available to me.\n\nThe Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections are unchanged and are in my previous reply."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":237,"cache_read_input_tokens":382218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":237},"output_tokens":546,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3e580ef-9188-4ffd-962e-28d451837174","uuid":"3ac35cad-55ce-4823-8ee9-baa55c2ed1df","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:37:17.403Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4H4pjV4Fk651WTdPYo"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The final reply does not contain the four required sections in this turn; it only says they are 'unchanged and are in my previous reply'. Also, the transcript shows TASK.md-required features that the build itself admits are not fully verified: the Xbox glyph option was never checked on real hardware, and the mouse controls were only just tested. The bundled .html and exit-interview.json exist and the JSON parses, but the stopping condition's requirement that the final reply contain all four sections is not met by the last message."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3e580ef-9188-4ffd-962e-28d451837174","uuid":"3a3a486d-175d-4989-ab48-ee9bc4d06c56","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:37:19.093Z","isSynthetic":true}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4HXPebaLdEqVUwouwJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is delivered: the single `ThugbyTurbo-Rugby-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-070002.html` is in the folder's root, and `exit-interview.json` parses with every field answered. `node test/all.mjs` passes all 126 checks across five suites, including the mouse test (hover finds a teammate, left click passes, right-button kick). I could not check the Xbox glyph option on real hardware. I did screenshot it and it renders.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 07:00:02\n- **Source:** rugby (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (Thugby Turbo, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade sports (rugby sevens, NBA Jam-style turbo). TV broadcast camera at a 40 degree pitch, switchable to a 55 degree three-quarter and a top-down view.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (Canvas 2D, Web Audio), AI Hub Session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, no other libraries, engine unmodified\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native HD pixel-art skeleton characters in team kits, procedural striped pitch with mud, stands with animated crowd, goalposts, sin-bin dumpster, venue weather and lights\n- **Animation:** the engine's Humanoid rig and E.MOVES, with new moves for rugby (tackle, big hit, pass, kick, fend, spin, sidestep) and poses for ruck, scrum, lineout lift, celebration and launched bodies\n- **Audio:** all music, effects and voices written in code: layered match music, whistles, hooter, crowd bed, hits, and Animalese-style babble voices\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel mode (each player plays their own match from the same seed, ranked by points margin); couch play for 1 to 2 players\n- **Testing:** headless simulation tests, scripted AI-vs-AI matches in all four venues, a scripted browser playthrough, headless Chromium checks including the mouse, and the AI Hub harness; no subagents\n- **Research:** PLAN.md, the engine README and API card plus engine source for Input.halfKeys, TileMap, Settings and audio, the AI Hub README, retrofit and session client; no web search\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown (no token or cost estimate was available to me)\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About eight:\n  - a stale phase handler running after a mid-step phase change (a crash)\n  - CPU set pieces waiting for scripted seats (an attract-mode stall)\n  - the kick-off handed to the wrong player\n  - invisible goalposts\n  - missing font glyphs for arrows and ticks\n  - an over-frequent interception and fumble rate\n  - a lost-keypress test bug\n  - a test helper that left the ball in the kick-off\n- **How many were critical?** Two: the phase-change crash and the attract-mode stall.\n- **Most helpful test:** full AI-vs-AI matches headless in all four venues, with a watchdog counter that fails on any stuck phase, plus direct scenario checks (tackle to ruck, monster hit, try to conversion to kick-off, scrum, lineout, penalty, cards, hazards).\n- **Least helpful test:** the AI Hub harness runs. They confirmed protocol compliance but passed first time and caught nothing. The screenshot sweeps only caught look problems a human would also see.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** characters that are data-driven 3D skeletons, where a new animation is one E.MOVES entry. The pause, settings, controls and rebinding screens come free, and the fixed-step `game.advance` made headless testing easy.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:**\n  - The pixel font has no arrow, tick or controller glyphs, so I drew badges with pixels.\n  - `px.line` with a width did not show for goalposts, but rects did.\n  - `Input.halfKeys` hands out buttons in preset order.\n  - The pointer coordinate space took a guess.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the whole match simulation (phases, laws, set pieces, referee sight, ball physics with the oval bounce, CPU brains), plus a 10-foot menu system and glyph badges.\n- **Hardest part:** fitting a rules state machine with many mini-games onto per-tick input edges and depth-sorted drawing. Every phase handler had to survive the phase changing mid-step.\n- **Engine changes:** none. The game adds its own broadcast view and E.MOVES entries from outside.\n- **One change I'd make:** add controller button and arrow glyphs to the font, and a team-sports phase kit (restarts, set pieces, a referee).\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the numbered plan with every rule and number written down, which turned design arguments into lookups. The one-command, failures-only testing instruction was also clear.\n- **Confusing:**\n  - The plan names different files and effort (opus max, 20261103) from the task (sonnet medium, 20261104), so I followed TASK.md.\n  - The plan assumes a shared-world hub session, while the task only says to follow the hub library.\n  - The plan is sized well beyond a medium-effort build.\n- **Hardest thing:** fitting a max-effort plan into one medium session and choosing what to simplify while keeping every listed feature present.\n- **What I'd change:** tier the plan into must, should and could; give the file-name convention once; say which hub mode is expected; say where usage numbers come from."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":861,"cache_read_input_tokens":382455,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":861},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3e580ef-9188-4ffd-962e-28d451837174","uuid":"8084d855-6439-4174-8cbf-9a944aa56e08","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:37:29.077Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4HWzM5ywBzpNdn5DAZ"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The final reply now contains all four sections, the HTML and exit-interview.json exist and the 126 checks pass. But the condition requires every TASK.md feature implemented, and the transcript does not establish that. The Xbox glyph option was never verified (the reply says so), and the mouse controls were only tested after the fact. TASK.md also asks for a dev mode with sliders for the most important gameplay variables, with a reset to defaults; the transcript shows TUNE sliders and a reset in dev mode, but the dev panel was only checked for opening, never for a changed slider value. Also, the reply's own admission that controls were not verified on real hardware leaves 'every feature implemented' unconfirmed, so the stopping condition is not clearly met."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3e580ef-9188-4ffd-962e-28d451837174","uuid":"a0a55555-2343-41f5-aa32-22a7d1b0645c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:37:31.531Z","isSynthetic":true}
