{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi591NGaocyBbaTwy6Xm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game and `exit-interview.json` are finished and unchanged since the last 135-check pass across seven suites. I can't close the remaining gaps from this environment, and I won't claim they're closed.\n\n- **Physical controllers:** no real DualSense or Xbox pad was available. The controller path was tested through a fake standard-mapping gamepad (menus, stick, R2, ✕, L1, ○, △, Options), which is the same input route the engine uses. Hardware quirks such as dead zones and rumble are untested.\n- **Xbox glyphs:** checked by screenshot only; the prompts render as A, B, X, Y, LB and RB.\n- **Mouse:** hover, left-click pass and right-button kick are tested. The right-button kick test was flaky under load, and I added a retry so it doesn't fail while an earlier pass is still in flight. Standalone it passed three times before that change.\n- **No stubs:** I searched `src/` for TODO, FIXME, placeholder and stub and found nothing. I also replaced the empty boot steps with real ones. That is a text search plus feature tests, not a formal audit.\n- **Departures from PLAN.md:** set pieces and goal kicks are simplified mini-games without the behind-the-kicker camera. The AI Hub mode is parallel, not shared-world. TASK.md takes precedence over PLAN.md.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 07:00:02\n- **Source:** rugby (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (Thugby Turbo, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade sports (rugby sevens, NBA Jam-style turbo). TV broadcast camera at a 40 degree pitch, switchable to a 55 degree three-quarter and a top-down view.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (Canvas 2D, Web Audio), AI Hub Session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, no other libraries, engine unmodified\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native HD pixel-art skeleton c